IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Part VIA, Division 3
-- "Obligations of person conducting relevant pet shop business" (ss 38G-38M)
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of Part VIA ("Pet shops and supply of dogs to relevant
-- pet shop businesses"), Division 3 (ss 38G-38M), as at the compilation
-- dated 28 Nov 2024 [version 08-b0-00], re-verified current 2026-09-09.
-- Source: lines 1324-1378 of mrdoc_47983.txt (western-australia/dog-act-1976
-- source bundle). This is a sibling encoding to dog-act-1976.l4 (Part VI
-- Divisions 1-2) and dog-act-part6a-div1-2-pet-shop-approval.l4 (Part VIA
-- Divisions 1-2) in this same directory; it imports the shared s. 3 domain
-- module (dog-act-domain.l4) for the Penalty record shape only -- this
-- Division's own actors (a person conducting a relevant pet shop business, a
-- local government) and facts are not shared with Part VI's dangerous-dog
-- material, so no LiableParty/DogProfile/AttackFacts value from that module
-- is read here.
--
-- All of Part VIA Division 3 was inserted by No. 29 of 2021 s. 32.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site with @ref, never expanded): s. 3 "relevant
-- pet shop business" (defined outside this line range); "pet shop
-- certificate" and "pet shop number" (Part VIA Division 1-2 machinery, a
-- different agent's assignment: dog-act-part6a-div1-2-pet-shop-approval.l4);
-- "dog supply approval" (created by Part VIA Division 4, ss 38N onwards,
-- outside ss 38G-38M -- a later section of the same Part this chunk does not
-- cover); "the regulations" prescribing a manner, form or time (delegated
-- subordinate legislation throughout, per this corpus's existing treatment
-- of "prescribed" facts, e.g. s. 33F(1) in dog-act-1976.l4).
-- =============================================================================

§ `Shared penalty presets and regulative-rule actors for this module`

-- Every stated Penalty in this Division is a flat fine with no minimum, no
-- imprisonment and no further-offence add-on (ss 38G, 38H, 38I, 38J, 38K(5),
-- 38L(4)) -- unlike Part VI Division 2's ss 33GA/33K penalties, none of
-- which carry a minimum-fine floor either way. One preset, parameterised by
-- amount, covers all six.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Penalty
`pet shop division 3 penalty of` amount MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST amount, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

-- The two genuine deadline-bearing duties in this Division (s 38K(4) and
-- s 38L(4)) share one small Party/Action vocabulary, local to this file per
-- this corpus's convention (dog-act-1976.l4's DogActParty/DogActAction are
-- not importable, and this Division's actors are different again).
DECLARE `Pet Shop Party` IS ONE OF
    `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business`
    `Local Government`

DECLARE `Pet Shop Action` IS ONE OF
    `make the record required by s 38K(2)`
    `provide record, information or evidence requested under s 38L(1)`

§ `Part VIA, Division 3 -- Obligations of person conducting relevant pet shop business`
§§ `38G. Relevant pet shop business only to supply dogs obtained from holder of dog supply approval`

DECLARE `Pet Shop Dog Supply Facts` HAS
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 3 "relevant pet shop business" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `a dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog was supplied to the relevant pet shop business by the holder of a dog supply approval` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) Part VIA Division 4 (ss 38N onwards) "dog supply approval" -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38G
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Dog Supply Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38G offence -- pet shop supplying a dog not obtained from a dog supply approval holder` f MEANS
        f's `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business`
    AND f's `a dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business`
    AND NOT f's `the dog was supplied to the relevant pet shop business by the holder of a dog supply approval`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38G Penalty
`s 38G penalty` MEANS `pet shop division 3 penalty of` 10_000

§§ `38H. Pet shop to display certificate of registration`

DECLARE `Pet Shop Certificate Display Facts` HAS
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 3 "relevant pet shop business" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `the pet shop certificate for the pet shop is displayed publicly at the pet shop` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) Part VIA Division 1-2 "pet shop certificate" -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38H
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Certificate Display Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38H offence -- pet shop certificate not displayed publicly` f MEANS
        f's `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business`
    AND NOT f's `the pet shop certificate for the pet shop is displayed publicly at the pet shop`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38H Penalty
`s 38H penalty` MEANS `pet shop division 3 penalty of` 5_000

§§ `38I. Person conducting relevant pet shop business to provide certain information`

DECLARE `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts` HAS
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 3 "relevant pet shop business" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38I(a)(i)-(ii); "prescribed information" and "pet shop number" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person requests the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person is provided with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38I(a)
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38I(a) obligation is met -- info to a person supplied with a dog` f MEANS
        (NOT f's `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business`)
    OR  f's `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38I(b)
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38I(b) obligation is met -- info to a person offered a dog, on request` f MEANS
        (NOT (   f's `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business`
              AND f's `that person requests the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number`))
    OR  f's `that person is provided with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38I
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38I offence -- failing to provide required information` f MEANS
        f's `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business`
    AND NOT (   `s 38I(a) obligation is met -- info to a person supplied with a dog` f
             AND `s 38I(b) obligation is met -- info to a person offered a dog, on request` f)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38I Penalty
`s 38I penalty` MEANS `pet shop division 3 penalty of` 5_000

§§ `38J. Person conducting relevant pet shop business to provide copy of health certificate`

DECLARE `Pet Shop Health Certificate Facts` HAS
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 3 "relevant pet shop business" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person requests a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person is provided with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38J(a)
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Health Certificate Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38J(a) obligation is met -- health certificate to a person supplied with a dog` f MEANS
        (NOT f's `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business`)
    OR  f's `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with a copy of the health certificate for the dog`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38J(b)
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Health Certificate Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38J(b) obligation is met -- health certificate to a person offered a dog, on request` f MEANS
        (NOT (   f's `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business`
              AND f's `that person requests a copy of the health certificate for the dog`))
    OR  f's `that person is provided with a copy of the health certificate for the dog`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38J
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Health Certificate Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38J offence -- failing to provide a copy of the health certificate` f MEANS
        f's `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business`
    AND NOT (   `s 38J(a) obligation is met -- health certificate to a person supplied with a dog` f
             AND `s 38J(b) obligation is met -- health certificate to a person offered a dog, on request` f)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38J Penalty
`s 38J penalty` MEANS `pet shop division 3 penalty of` 5_000

§§ `38K. Person conducting relevant pet shop business to keep records relating to source of dogs`

-- s 38K(1) -- a pure definitional provision ("relevant dog ... means each of
-- the following"): the two limbs are DISJUNCTIVE ("each of the following"),
-- so a single dog may satisfy both at once (kept for the business for a
-- while, then later supplied). See the F-38K3B-RETENTION-CUMULATIVE
-- ambiguity below, which turns on exactly this.
DECLARE `Relevant Dog Facts` HAS
    `dog is kept for the purposes of the relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38K(1)
GIVEN dog IS A `Relevant Dog Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog is a relevant dog for the purposes of s 38K` dog MEANS
        dog's `dog is kept for the purposes of the relevant pet shop business`
    OR  dog's `dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business`

-- REVIEW FIX: s 38K(3)'s chapeau ("The person must keep the record, EVEN IF
-- the person ceases to conduct the relevant pet shop business") explicitly
-- extends the recordkeeping duty (and so the s 38K(5) offence) past
-- cessation -- unlike ss 38G/H/I/J, which have no such extension and so
-- correctly keep the narrower "conducts" actor gate. This record's actor
-- gate therefore mirrors s 38L(1)'s own "conducts or has conducted" wording
-- rather than duplicating the narrower gate used elsewhere in this file.
DECLARE `Pet Shop Recordkeeping Facts` HAS
    `the person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 3 "relevant pet shop business" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `at least one relevant dog exists in relation to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a record was kept for each relevant dog, containing the prescribed information including information about the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record includes evidence necessary to verify the information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record was kept in the prescribed way, if any is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record was kept until the end of the applicable retention period under s 38K(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record was made within any time prescribed under s 38K(4)` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38K(2)-(3)
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Recordkeeping Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38K(2)-(3) recordkeeping obligation is met` f MEANS
        (NOT f's `at least one relevant dog exists in relation to the person`)
    OR  (   f's `a record was kept for each relevant dog, containing the prescribed information including information about the supplier`
        AND f's `the record includes evidence necessary to verify the information`
        AND f's `the record was kept in the prescribed way, if any is prescribed`
        AND f's `the record was kept until the end of the applicable retention period under s 38K(3)(b)`)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38K(5)
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Recordkeeping Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38K offence -- failing to comply with recordkeeping requirements` f MEANS
        f's `the person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business`
    AND NOT (   `s 38K(2)-(3) recordkeeping obligation is met` f
             AND f's `the record was made within any time prescribed under s 38K(4)`)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38K(5) Penalty
`s 38K penalty` MEANS `pet shop division 3 penalty of` 10_000

-- AMBIGUITY (F-38K3B-RETENTION-CUMULATIVE): s 38K(1) defines "relevant dog"
-- disjunctively -- "each of the following": (a) kept for the business's
-- purposes; (b) supplied or offered for supply -- so a single dog can
-- satisfy both limbs (e.g. kept for the business for a period, then later
-- supplied). s 38K(3)(b) then states the retention deadline as two
-- sub-limbs, (i) and (ii), one per s 38K(1) limb, joined by "and". Question:
-- for a dog that is a relevant dog under BOTH limbs, must the record be kept
-- until the LATER of the two five-year windows (the "and" read
-- cumulatively across the sub-limbs), or does only the sub-limb matching
-- whichever characterisation currently applies govern? Taken reading:
-- cumulative -- retention is required for as long as EITHER applicable
-- sub-period has not yet run, i.e. until the later of the two dates where
-- both limbs apply. Rejected: only the "current" characterisation's
-- sub-limb governs, letting a later characterisation reset or shorten an
-- already-running retention clock. (This mirrors the "and"-joined,
-- per-limb-deadline shape of s 38K(1) itself, which this file's
-- disjunctive `the dog is a relevant dog for the purposes of s 38K` already
-- takes as inclusive-or.)
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38K(3)(b)
GIVEN `dog is a relevant dog under s 38K(1)(a) (kept for the purposes of the business)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years elapsed since the dog ceased being kept for those purposes` IS A NUMBER,
      `dog is a relevant dog under s 38K(1)(b) (supplied or offered for supply)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years elapsed since the dog was supplied or first offered for supply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person must still retain the s 38K(2) record for this dog` `dog is a relevant dog under s 38K(1)(a) (kept for the purposes of the business)` `years elapsed since the dog ceased being kept for those purposes` `dog is a relevant dog under s 38K(1)(b) (supplied or offered for supply)` `years elapsed since the dog was supplied or first offered for supply` MEANS
        (   `dog is a relevant dog under s 38K(1)(a) (kept for the purposes of the business)`
        AND `years elapsed since the dog ceased being kept for those purposes` LESS THAN 5)
    OR  (   `dog is a relevant dog under s 38K(1)(b) (supplied or offered for supply)`
        AND `years elapsed since the dog was supplied or first offered for supply` LESS THAN 5)

-- s 38K(4)'s duty has no numeric deadline of its own in the Act -- the
-- deadline exists only IF the regulations prescribe one. Modelled as a
-- MAYBE NUMBER input (unit: days, by this file's convention, matching
-- dog-act-1976.l4's s 33K(2)/(3) 24-hour duties): NOTHING when no time is
-- prescribed (no duty arises at all, per the section's own "if" clause),
-- JUST days when one is.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38K(4)
GIVEN `time to make the record, in days, if a time is prescribed under s 38K(4)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Pet Shop Party` `Pet Shop Action`
`s 38K(4) duty to make the record within the prescribed time` `time to make the record, in days, if a time is prescribed under s 38K(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `time to make the record, in days, if a time is prescribed under s 38K(4)`
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN JUST days THEN
        PARTY `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business`
        MUST  `make the record required by s 38K(2)`
        WITHIN days
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST  BREACH BY `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business`
              BECAUSE "the record required by s 38K(2) was not made within the time prescribed under s 38K(4)"

§§ `38L. Person conducting relevant pet shop business to provide information to local government`

DECLARE `Local Government Request Eligibility Facts` HAS
    `person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 3 "relevant pet shop business" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `the pet shop for the relevant pet shop business is or was located in the local government's district` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38L(1)
GIVEN f IS A `Local Government Request Eligibility Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government may make a s 38L(1) request` f MEANS
        f's `person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business`
    AND f's `the pet shop for the relevant pet shop business is or was located in the local government's district`

-- s 38L(2) -- the local government may take extracts from, or make copies
-- of, any record, information or evidence provided under a s 38L(1)
-- request. Purely administrative machinery: no fact any rule in this file,
-- or elsewhere in this corpus, would test turns on whether extracts or
-- copies were taken, so it is recorded here as inert prose rather than a
-- force-fit predicate.

DECLARE `Pet Shop Information Request` HAS
    `specifies the time within which the record, information or evidence must be provided` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38L(3)
GIVEN n IS A `Pet Shop Information Request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 38L(1) request satisfies its content requirements` n MEANS
    n's `specifies the time within which the record, information or evidence must be provided`

-- s 38L(4)'s deadline is either the time specified in the request, or (if
-- the local government and the person later agree a different time) that
-- agreed time instead. Pulled out as its own named function so the
-- resolution rule is independently testable, not just buried inside the
-- WITHIN clause below.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38L(4)
GIVEN `time specified in the request, in days` IS A NUMBER,
      `time later agreed between the local government and the person, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the effective time to comply under s 38L(4), in days` `time specified in the request, in days` `time later agreed between the local government and the person, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `time later agreed between the local government and the person, if any`
    WHEN JUST agreedDays THEN agreedDays
    WHEN NOTHING         THEN `time specified in the request, in days`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38L(4)
GIVEN `time specified in the request, in days` IS A NUMBER,
      `time later agreed between the local government and the person, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Pet Shop Party` `Pet Shop Action`
`s 38L(4) duty to comply with a s 38L(1) request` `time specified in the request, in days` `time later agreed between the local government and the person, if any` MEANS
    PARTY `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business`
    MUST  `provide record, information or evidence requested under s 38L(1)`
    WITHIN (`the effective time to comply under s 38L(4), in days` `time specified in the request, in days` `time later agreed between the local government and the person, if any`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business`
          BECAUSE "the record, information or evidence requested under s 38L(1) was not provided within the time required"

DECLARE `Pet Shop Information Request Compliance Facts` HAS
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 3 "relevant pet shop business" -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `a request was made under s 38L(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the record, information or evidence was provided within the time specified in the request, or any later agreed time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- REVIEW FIX: the @ref citing "s. 38L(4) Penalty" previously sat above this
-- offence predicate, leaving `s 38L penalty` below with no @ref of its own
-- -- inconsistent with every other offence/Penalty pair in this file (each
-- of which gives the offence predicate its own plain @ref, and the Penalty
-- value its own "... Penalty" @ref). Split the two annotations apart to
-- match.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38L(4)
GIVEN f IS A `Pet Shop Information Request Compliance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38L offence -- failing to comply with a s 38L(1) request in time` f MEANS
        f's `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business`
    AND f's `a request was made under s 38L(1)`
    AND NOT f's `the record, information or evidence was provided within the time specified in the request, or any later agreed time`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38L(4) Penalty
`s 38L penalty` MEANS `pet shop division 3 penalty of` 10_000

§§ `38M. Self-incrimination`

-- s 38M(1) abolishes the privilege against self-incrimination as an excuse
-- for non-compliance with a s 38L request, absolutely -- it is not a
-- conditional test, so this is a plain constant fact rather than a
-- predicate over some claimed excuse.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38M(1)
`self-incrimination excuses non-compliance with a s 38L request` MEANS FALSE

-- REVIEW FIX: s 38M(2) excludes compelled evidence only "in any proceedings
-- for an offence other than proceedings for an offence against this Act or
-- for perjury" -- the exclusion's scope is proceedings FOR AN OFFENCE in the
-- first place. The originally drafted predicate omitted that gate and so
-- would (wrongly) treat compelled evidence as inadmissible in ANY
-- proceedings that are not for an Act offence or perjury, including a
-- non-offence (e.g. civil) proceeding s 38M(2) does not purport to touch.
-- Added `the proceedings are for an offence` as the missing gate.
DECLARE `Compelled Disclosure Admissibility Facts` HAS
    `the record, information or evidence was provided by an individual in compliance with a request under s 38L` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are for an offence against this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are for perjury` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38M(2)
GIVEN f IS A `Compelled Disclosure Admissibility Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the record, information or evidence is admissible against the individual in the proceedings` f MEANS
        (NOT f's `the record, information or evidence was provided by an individual in compliance with a request under s 38L`)
    OR  (NOT f's `the proceedings are for an offence`)
    OR  f's `the proceedings are for an offence against this Act`
    OR  f's `the proceedings are for perjury`

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

-- s 38G
`s 38G facts -- dog from an unapproved source` MEANS `Pet Shop Dog Supply Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `the dog was supplied to the relevant pet shop business by the holder of a dog supply approval` IS FALSE

`s 38G facts -- dog from an approved source` MEANS `Pet Shop Dog Supply Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `the dog was supplied to the relevant pet shop business by the holder of a dog supply approval` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 38G offence -- pet shop supplying a dog not obtained from a dog supply approval holder` `s 38G facts -- dog from an unapproved source`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 38G offence -- pet shop supplying a dog not obtained from a dog supply approval holder` `s 38G facts -- dog from an approved source`)
#ASSERT `s 38G penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

-- s 38H
`s 38H facts -- certificate not displayed` MEANS `Pet Shop Certificate Display Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `the pet shop certificate for the pet shop is displayed publicly at the pet shop` IS FALSE

`s 38H facts -- certificate displayed` MEANS `Pet Shop Certificate Display Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `the pet shop certificate for the pet shop is displayed publicly at the pet shop` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 38H offence -- pet shop certificate not displayed publicly` `s 38H facts -- certificate not displayed`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 38H offence -- pet shop certificate not displayed publicly` `s 38H facts -- certificate displayed`)

-- s 38I
`s 38I facts -- both limbs complied with` MEANS `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS TRUE
    , `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person requests the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS TRUE
    , `that person is provided with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS TRUE

`s 38I facts -- supplied person not given info before supply` MEANS `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE
    , `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE
    , `that person requests the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE
    , `that person is provided with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE

`s 38I facts -- offered person requested but not given info` MEANS `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE
    , `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE
    , `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person requests the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS TRUE
    , `that person is provided with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE

`s 38I facts -- offered person did not request, none given` MEANS `Pet Shop Purchaser Information Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE
    , `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE
    , `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person requests the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE
    , `that person is provided with the prescribed information about the supplier and the pet shop number` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`s 38I offence -- failing to provide required information` `s 38I facts -- both limbs complied with`)
#ASSERT `s 38I offence -- failing to provide required information` `s 38I facts -- supplied person not given info before supply`
#ASSERT `s 38I offence -- failing to provide required information` `s 38I facts -- offered person requested but not given info`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 38I offence -- failing to provide required information` `s 38I facts -- offered person did not request, none given`)
#ASSERT `s 38I penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

-- s 38J
`s 38J facts -- both limbs complied with` MEANS `Pet Shop Health Certificate Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS TRUE
    , `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person requests a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS TRUE
    , `that person is provided with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS TRUE

`s 38J facts -- supplied person not given certificate before supply` MEANS `Pet Shop Health Certificate Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS FALSE
    , `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE
    , `that person requests a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS FALSE
    , `that person is provided with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS FALSE

`s 38J facts -- offered person did not request, none given` MEANS `Pet Shop Health Certificate Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a person is supplied with a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE
    , `that person is provided, before the dog is supplied, with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS FALSE
    , `a person is offered the supply of a dog in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `that person requests a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS FALSE
    , `that person is provided with a copy of the health certificate for the dog` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`s 38J offence -- failing to provide a copy of the health certificate` `s 38J facts -- both limbs complied with`)
#ASSERT `s 38J offence -- failing to provide a copy of the health certificate` `s 38J facts -- supplied person not given certificate before supply`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 38J offence -- failing to provide a copy of the health certificate` `s 38J facts -- offered person did not request, none given`)
#ASSERT `s 38J penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

-- s 38K
`a dog kept for the business only` MEANS `Relevant Dog Facts` WITH
    `dog is kept for the purposes of the relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE

`a dog neither kept nor supplied` MEANS `Relevant Dog Facts` WITH
    `dog is kept for the purposes of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE
    , `dog is supplied or offered for supply in the course of the relevant pet shop business` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the dog is a relevant dog for the purposes of s 38K` `a dog kept for the business only`
#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is a relevant dog for the purposes of s 38K` `a dog neither kept nor supplied`)

-- F-38K3B-RETENTION-CUMULATIVE witness: a dog that ceased being kept for the
-- business's purposes 4 years ago (limb (a)'s window not yet expired) and
-- was ALSO supplied 6 years ago (limb (b)'s window expired) -- must still be
-- retained, because limb (a)'s window has not yet run.
#ASSERT `the person must still retain the s 38K(2) record for this dog` TRUE 4 TRUE 6
#ASSERT NOT (`the person must still retain the s 38K(2) record for this dog` TRUE 6 TRUE 6)

`s 38K facts -- fully compliant` MEANS `Pet Shop Recordkeeping Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `at least one relevant dog exists in relation to the person` IS TRUE
    , `a record was kept for each relevant dog, containing the prescribed information including information about the supplier` IS TRUE
    , `the record includes evidence necessary to verify the information` IS TRUE
    , `the record was kept in the prescribed way, if any is prescribed` IS TRUE
    , `the record was kept until the end of the applicable retention period under s 38K(3)(b)` IS TRUE
    , `the record was made within any time prescribed under s 38K(4)` IS TRUE

`s 38K facts -- no record kept at all` MEANS `Pet Shop Recordkeeping Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `at least one relevant dog exists in relation to the person` IS TRUE
    , `a record was kept for each relevant dog, containing the prescribed information including information about the supplier` IS FALSE
    , `the record includes evidence necessary to verify the information` IS FALSE
    , `the record was kept in the prescribed way, if any is prescribed` IS FALSE
    , `the record was kept until the end of the applicable retention period under s 38K(3)(b)` IS FALSE
    , `the record was made within any time prescribed under s 38K(4)` IS FALSE

-- REVIEW FIX witness: s 38K(3) keeps the retention duty alive "even if the
-- person ceases to conduct the relevant pet shop business" -- a person who
-- has ceased trading but let the retention period lapse early still commits
-- the s 38K(5) offence; this is only reachable once the actor gate reads
-- "conducts or has conducted" rather than "conducts".
`s 38K facts -- ceased trading, retention period not honoured` MEANS `Pet Shop Recordkeeping Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `at least one relevant dog exists in relation to the person` IS TRUE
    , `a record was kept for each relevant dog, containing the prescribed information including information about the supplier` IS TRUE
    , `the record includes evidence necessary to verify the information` IS TRUE
    , `the record was kept in the prescribed way, if any is prescribed` IS TRUE
    , `the record was kept until the end of the applicable retention period under s 38K(3)(b)` IS FALSE
    , `the record was made within any time prescribed under s 38K(4)` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT (`s 38K offence -- failing to comply with recordkeeping requirements` `s 38K facts -- fully compliant`)
#ASSERT `s 38K offence -- failing to comply with recordkeeping requirements` `s 38K facts -- no record kept at all`
#ASSERT `s 38K offence -- failing to comply with recordkeeping requirements` `s 38K facts -- ceased trading, retention period not honoured`
#ASSERT `s 38K penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

#TRACE `s 38K(4) duty to make the record within the prescribed time` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1)
-- Result: FULFILLED (no time prescribed under s 38K(4) -- no duty arises)

#TRACE `s 38K(4) duty to make the record within the prescribed time` (JUST 10) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business` DOES `make the record required by s 38K(2)` AT 5
-- Result: FULFILLED (record made within the 10-day prescribed time)

#TRACE `s 38K(4) duty to make the record within the prescribed time` (JUST 10) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- no record made within the 10-day prescribed time

-- s 38L
`s 38L1 facts -- pet shop in the district` MEANS `Local Government Request Eligibility Facts` WITH
    `person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `the pet shop for the relevant pet shop business is or was located in the local government's district` IS TRUE

`s 38L1 facts -- pet shop outside the district` MEANS `Local Government Request Eligibility Facts` WITH
    `person conducts or has conducted a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `the pet shop for the relevant pet shop business is or was located in the local government's district` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the local government may make a s 38L(1) request` `s 38L1 facts -- pet shop in the district`
#ASSERT NOT (`the local government may make a s 38L(1) request` `s 38L1 facts -- pet shop outside the district`)

`a compliant s 38L(1) request` MEANS `Pet Shop Information Request` WITH `specifies the time within which the record, information or evidence must be provided` IS TRUE
`a non-compliant s 38L(1) request` MEANS `Pet Shop Information Request` WITH `specifies the time within which the record, information or evidence must be provided` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the s 38L(1) request satisfies its content requirements` `a compliant s 38L(1) request`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 38L(1) request satisfies its content requirements` `a non-compliant s 38L(1) request`)

#ASSERT `the effective time to comply under s 38L(4), in days` 14 NOTHING EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the effective time to comply under s 38L(4), in days` 14 (JUST 20) EQUALS 20

`s 38L facts -- complied in time` MEANS `Pet Shop Information Request Compliance Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a request was made under s 38L(1)` IS TRUE
    , `the record, information or evidence was provided within the time specified in the request, or any later agreed time` IS TRUE

`s 38L facts -- not complied in time` MEANS `Pet Shop Information Request Compliance Facts` WITH
    `the person conducts a relevant pet shop business` IS TRUE
    , `a request was made under s 38L(1)` IS TRUE
    , `the record, information or evidence was provided within the time specified in the request, or any later agreed time` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`s 38L offence -- failing to comply with a s 38L(1) request in time` `s 38L facts -- complied in time`)
#ASSERT `s 38L offence -- failing to comply with a s 38L(1) request in time` `s 38L facts -- not complied in time`
#ASSERT `s 38L penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

#TRACE `s 38L(4) duty to comply with a s 38L(1) request` 14 NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business` DOES `provide record, information or evidence requested under s 38L(1)` AT 10
-- Result: FULFILLED (provided within the 14-day specified time)

#TRACE `s 38L(4) duty to comply with a s 38L(1) request` 14 NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 15)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- not provided within the 14-day specified time

#TRACE `s 38L(4) duty to comply with a s 38L(1) request` 5 (JUST 20) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Person Conducting The Relevant Pet Shop Business` DOES `provide record, information or evidence requested under s 38L(1)` AT 18
-- Result: FULFILLED -- the agreed 20-day time overrides the 5-day time
-- originally specified in the request

-- s 38M
#ASSERT NOT `self-incrimination excuses non-compliance with a s 38L request`

`s 38M2 facts -- compelled disclosure, Act offence proceedings` MEANS `Compelled Disclosure Admissibility Facts` WITH
    `the record, information or evidence was provided by an individual in compliance with a request under s 38L` IS TRUE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence` IS TRUE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence against this Act` IS TRUE
    , `the proceedings are for perjury` IS FALSE

`s 38M2 facts -- compelled disclosure, unrelated offence proceedings` MEANS `Compelled Disclosure Admissibility Facts` WITH
    `the record, information or evidence was provided by an individual in compliance with a request under s 38L` IS TRUE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence` IS TRUE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence against this Act` IS FALSE
    , `the proceedings are for perjury` IS FALSE

-- REVIEW FIX witness: s 38M(2)'s exclusion only reaches proceedings FOR AN
-- OFFENCE -- compelled disclosure used against the individual in a civil
-- (non-offence) proceeding is not touched by this subsection at all, and so
-- remains admissible. This case was unreachable before the missing gate was
-- added (a bare "not an Act offence, not perjury" test wrongly caught it).
`s 38M2 facts -- compelled disclosure, non-offence (civil) proceedings` MEANS `Compelled Disclosure Admissibility Facts` WITH
    `the record, information or evidence was provided by an individual in compliance with a request under s 38L` IS TRUE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence` IS FALSE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence against this Act` IS FALSE
    , `the proceedings are for perjury` IS FALSE

`s 38M2 facts -- not compelled disclosure` MEANS `Compelled Disclosure Admissibility Facts` WITH
    `the record, information or evidence was provided by an individual in compliance with a request under s 38L` IS FALSE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence` IS TRUE
    , `the proceedings are for an offence against this Act` IS FALSE
    , `the proceedings are for perjury` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the record, information or evidence is admissible against the individual in the proceedings` `s 38M2 facts -- compelled disclosure, Act offence proceedings`
#ASSERT NOT (`the record, information or evidence is admissible against the individual in the proceedings` `s 38M2 facts -- compelled disclosure, unrelated offence proceedings`)
#ASSERT `the record, information or evidence is admissible against the individual in the proceedings` `s 38M2 facts -- compelled disclosure, non-offence (civil) proceedings`
#ASSERT `the record, information or evidence is admissible against the individual in the proceedings` `s 38M2 facts -- not compelled disclosure`
